This run is a warning against extrapolating a remembered ray rule from task ID or superficial diagonals. Inputs varied substantially: an unchanged compact multicolor cluster; a demo with two diagonal trails; a bg7 marker configuration whose output extended 2 up-right and 5 down-left; and a bg1 test with 9/7/6 marks. Multiple predicted extensions on the test were wrong. Even several demonstrations did not validate which test markers trigger rays. Match the local arrangement, orientation, and marker roles in a demonstration before extending; a pair alone does not establish direction or applicability. After rejection, do not rotate/recolor the guessed ray as a cosmetic retry. Spend another demo only if it can address a named ambiguity in comparable geometry.
